  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q10-content",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The graph of $y=\\ln(4-2x)$ is $y=\\ln(-2x)$ translated by how many units and in which direction?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Translated right by 2 units.",
      "worked": "Let $a$ be the signed rightward translation. Replace $x$ with $x-a$ in the original rule.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\ln(-2(x-a))\\\\y&=\\ln(-2x+2a)\\end{align*}$$\n\nCompare the arguments with the new rule.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-2x+2a&=4-2x\\\\2a&=4\\\\a&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, the graph is translated 2 units right.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
